etween Mr. Drabinsky and Cineplex 's major shareholder , MCA Inc. MCA and Cineplex 's other major shareholder , Montreal-based financier Charles Bronfman and his associates , have <ei32 agreed> to <ei33 tender> their holdings to an offer by Mr. Drabinsky unless a higher offer is <ei34 made> by another bidder . MCA holds half of Cineplex 's equity and 33 % of its voting rights through restricted voting shares , while Bronfman interests hold about 24 % of the company 's equity . Ms. Kolber <ei35 said> the committee had <ei36 received> other bids . She <ei37 declined> to <ei38 identify> other bidders but <ei39 said> Mr. Drabinsky 's offer \" is all cash , and it 's for all of the company . \" Several Cineplex analysts have <ei40 speculated> that outside bids received by the committee were either disappointingly <ei41 low> or for only part of the company . \" All this has really established is that MCA and the Bronfmans have <ei42 agreed> on a price at which they can be <ei43 bought> out , \" <ei44 said> Jeffery Logsdon , an analyst with Crowell , Weedon in Los Angeles . \" If a bid <ei45 materializes> at that price , shareholders will have every reason to be <ei46 glad> , but the question of financing still <ei47 remains> . \" Last April , Mr. Drabinsky and a group of financial backers <ei49 planned> to <ei50 acquire> up to 30.2 % of Cineplex for C $ 17.50 a share from Bronfman associates . Mr. Drabinsky , who would have <ei51 had> the right to <ei52 vote> those shares for two years , <ei54 said> the <ei55 purchase> , subsequently <ei56 rejected> by regulators , was <ei57 aimed> at <ei58 consolidating> his control of the company . MCA strongly <ei59 opposed> the Drabinsky group 's move . The directors did n't <ei60 indicate> the source of financing for Mr. Drabinsky 's new proposal , but <ei61 said> MCA and the Bronfman associates <ei62 agreed> in principle to <ei63 buy> for $ 57 million and then <ei64 lease> back to Cineplex its 18-screen theater complex in Universal City , Calif . , if Mr. Drabinsky <ei65 succeeds> in an offer . \" This is being <ei66 done> at the <ei67 suggestion> of { Mr . Drabinsky } and to <ei68 accommodate> him , to <ei69 facilitate> his financing <ei70 arrangements> , \" Ms. Kolber <ei71 said> . In addition , the directors <ei72 said> if a bid by Mr. Drabinsky is <ei73 successful> , Cineplex <ei74 expects> Rank Organisation PLC to <ei75 acquire> the 51 % of Cineplex 's Film House unit it does n't <ei76 own> , and <ei77 provide> Mr. Drabinsky with additional loan financing . Michael Gifford , Rank 's chief executive , <ei78 said> the British theater chain 's total involvement \" would n't <ei79 exceed> $ 100 million \" but <ei80 declined> to <ei81 give> a breakdown between the loan financing and the proposed Film House purchase . Cineplex shareholders <ei82 responded> coolly to yesterday 's <ei84 announcement> . In <ei85 trading> on the New York Stock Exchange , Cineplex <ei86 closed> at $ 11 , down 25 cents , with more than a million shares changing hands . On the Toronto Stock Exchange , Cineplex <ei87 closed> at C $ 12.875 , off 37.5 Canadian cents , well below the C $ 16.40 level . \" Where 's the bid ? \" asked Pierre Panet - Raymond , an analyst and broker with Toronto securities dealer McDermid St. Lawrence Ltd. Mr. Panet - Raymond <ei88 said> he does n't <ei89 think> Messrs . Drabinsky and Gottlieb are \" anywhere <ei90 close> \" to <ei91 arranging> <ei92 financing> and that investors will <ei93 need> a solid <ei94 offer> before the stock <ei95 begins> to <ei96 rise> again . Mr. Drabinsky could n't be <ei97 reached> for comment .", "gold": [["ei31", "causes", "ei28"], ["ei31", "causes", "ei29"], ["ei28", "causedby", "ei31"], ["ei29", "causedby", "ei31"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei23", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei28", "ei29", "ei31", "ei3